      "id": 1,
      "text": "Regis Falls was formally established in the 1850s, named for the scenic waterfalls on the St. River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/st_regis_falls_new_york"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "By the 1880s, lumbermen like Peter Macfarlane modernized mills, boosting output from 3–4 million to tens of millions of board feet per year.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/st_regis_falls_new_york"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Northern Adirondack Railroad linked the village to Moira in 1883, turning Saint Regis Falls into a lumber‑haul hub.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9,
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.townofwaverlyny.org/about"
    },
    {
